            <div xml:id="d485">

                <pb facs="0609" n="515" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg515"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.001C13/82: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-14T14:00:00-05:00">December 14, 1929—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>541. Department informed by Chief of Staff that he has arranged for armed guard
                    to escort General Calles’ party across Mexican border. <pb facs="0610" n="516"
                        xml:id="pg516"/> Ambassador Téllez is a member of party. General Calles
                    plans to leave New York 6:50 this evening arriving St. Louis 5:10 Sunday
                    evening, leaving immediately from there by special train for Laredo.</p>
                <p>In view of urgency of matter Department has proceeded with arrangements without
                    obtaining permission from Mexican Government for armed troops to enter Mexico.
                    Please explain matter to Acting Minister of Foreign Affairs and telegraph his
                    acquiescence.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
